Thank you very much for your reply, Andy,
I was not going to use the model with all variables but use the "dredge" to create models with all possible combinations of those variables (from 1 to n covariates) and then use the "occu" for the occupancy models. I usually use this approach with logistic regression always using presence data;

model <-glm (presencedata ~ all variables, family = binomial, data = data)
dd <-dredge (model, subset = subs)

where in "subs" imposed which variables should not come together in the model because they related to each other.

and finally

model.avg (get.models (dd, delta <4))

do you think it is possible to use something with unmarked?

the few detections are due to the low density of the species (wolf) and the type of monitoring program on a large scale ..

best regards

matteo

