Hi Jim, that's great. Did you use unmarked to estimate the parameters? I'm a little bit surprised by how often you got estimates of psi=1 when p was low. I realize that there is a ridge in the likelihood when p is low, but I'm guessing that the optimizer wasn't finding the global optimum in most of these cases. Have you tried using method="Nelder-Mead" and/or better starting values?

FWIW, Dave Miller has been encouraging me to add a simplex algorithm to find better starting values, which is a great idea, but I haven't had time.

Richard

