No, I used a program I wrote.  However, I did use Equation (1) in Guillera-Arroita, et. al. (2014) http://www.plosone.org/article/info%3Adoi%2F10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0099571 that gives the condition for which the mle of psi is exactly 1.0.

Attached is some R code (not what I used to create the animated gifs) that will calculate the probability the the mle of psi is exactly 1.0 for any combination of number of sites, visits, psi, and p using simulations.  For 55 sites, 2 visits per site, psi = 0.25, and p = 0.10, the probability of the mle of psi being 1 is around 0.80.  (Not that anyone would expect to get good estimates of psi with such parameter values for any estimation method.)

When I do use occu in unmarked I do use method="Nelder-Mead" as you suggested a short time ago.  That fixed all of the issues I was having with occu.

Jim

